   {"q": "Why should victims of an undepletable externality not be taxed or subsidised?", "a": "Because the externality is non-rival: a victim's defensive action does not change anyone else's exposure. They already bear the full marginal damage they suffer, so their private incentive to undertake preventative activity is already socially optimal. Adding a tax or subsidy causes over-deterrence. Only the generator should face the fee.", "difficulty": "advanced"},
